## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design joint monocular depth and motion estimation under dynamic scenes and adverse weather, optimized for edge devices and quick adaptation to new conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth and scene-flow fusion in cluttered traffic
- Temporal fusion across frames for stability
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with lightweight adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture sketch
function forward(x) {
  const z = encoder(x); // shared features
  const d = depthHead(z);
  const s = flowHead(z);
  const o = objMotionHead(z);
  const t = temporalFuse([d, s, o]);
  return {depth: d, sceneFlow: s, objectMotion: o, fused: t};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure edge-device latency vs. accuracy across weather scenarios?
- Which datasets and metrics would you prioritize for evaluation and validation?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses multi-sensor fusion design with real-time constraints in a practical logistics setting.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-sensor fusion (stereo, LiDAR, IMU)
- Data association under occlusion (JPDA/MHT)
- Real-time edge latency and lightweight models
- Track management and drift handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: simple UKF update step with JPDA associations
function updateUKF(state, measurements, associations) {
  // Predict step using motion model
  const predicted = predictState(state);

  // JPDA-weighted measurement update
  const innovation = computeInnovation(predicted, measurements);
  const kalmanGain = computeKalmanGain(predicted.covariance, innovation.covariance);

  // Apply JPDA-weighted update
  const updatedState = applyUpdate(state, innovation, kalmanGain, associations.weights);

  return updatedState;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to handle equipment with strong reflective/transparent surfaces, a realistic industrial setting, and on-device adaptation under tight latency budgets.

## Key Concepts
- Reflective/transparent object pose estimation
- Differentiable rendering for photometric consistency
- On-device 3-shot adaptation via compact adapters
- Synthetic+real data with material randomization
- Edge latency and robustness under glare

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch
function forward(frame) {
  const feats = backbone(frame);
  const seg = segHead(feats);
  const pose = poseHead(feats);
  const render = differentiableRenderer(pose, frame);
  return {seg, pose, loss: computeLoss(render, frame)};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt to varying refractive indices?
- How would you quantify uncertainty in pose under specular highlights?

